Trace each kmem claim on both sides of vm_map_locate_space

The startup token [13.0] is kmem_range_init and the last claim printed is 9 of 17,
so the boot hangs inside vm_map_locate_space for that claim.  Print the claim's
size, range pointer and name before the call and the address it chose after it:
the next boot then separates a hang inside the search from a hang after it, and
shows whether the claim descriptor itself is garbage.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
index 2927d4b..d0c007e 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -3546,6 +3546,8 @@ kmem_scramble_ranges(void)
 {
